  [PASS] 118F the arm-class test cannot be done on this sample and says so: only 5 SPARC galaxies in the S4G catalogue are grand-design spirals, so the smallest offset difference detectable at 2 sigma against the flocculent class is 0.11 dex -- as large as the whole between-galaxy scatter.  Recorded as underpowered, not as a null   (N(grand design) = 5, N(flocculent) = 18, N(multiple-arm) = 24; detectable offset difference 0.105 dex against a between-galaxy scatter of 0.104 dex)

